<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

  <%= erb :_head %>

  <body>
    <div class="wrapper">

      <%= erb :_logo %>

      <h2>MCP Tools: flair-gg-vp-server</h2>

      <p>
        This is the tool catalogue for the Model Context Protocol (MCP) endpoint at
        <code><%= request.path %></code>. An MCP client (e.g. an LLM agent) talks to
        this same URL via JSON-RPC 2.0 <code>POST</code> requests
        (<code>initialize</code>, <code>tools/list</code>, <code>tools/call</code>).
        This page is a human-readable view of the same tool list, generated from
        <code>lib/mcp_tools/</code> - one file per tool - so it can never drift
        from what the server actually offers.
      </p>

      <% @tools.each do |tool| %>
        <div style="border: 1px solid #ccc; border-radius: 6px; padding: 1em; margin-bottom: 1.5em;">
          <h3><code><%= tool[:name] %></code></h3>
          <pre style="white-space: pre-wrap;"><%= tool[:description] %></pre>
          <h4>Input schema</h4>
          <pre><%= JSON.pretty_generate(tool[:inputSchema]) %></pre>
        </div>
      <% end %>

    <%= erb :_footer %>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
